      "content": "hey, i'm an architect and i've been noticing something weird in this new high-rise development i'm working in. the HVAC and smart lighting systems have this rhythmic pulsing, it's almost sub-audible but i can feel it when i'm sitting still. it's making everyone in the unit feel super jittery and anxious. do you think it's possible they're using specific low-frequency oscillations for some kind of behavioral modulation? i need to figure out if there's a pattern.",
