      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's what i was thinking. it feels way too intentional to be a coincidence, especially with how much \"smart\" tech is integrated into the grid here. i've been trying to map it out with a spectrum analyzer on my phone but the readings are messy because of the interference. if they are actually using frequencies to modulate mood or compliance, how would one even go about detecting the specific Hz range they're targeting? like, is there a way to isolate the signal from the standard mechanical noise of the HVAC?",
